Answer: The local variable takes priority when the name is used without qualification. For example:

```java
class Product {
int id;
```

Product(int id) {

```java
id = id;
}
}
```

Both occurrences of id are interpreted as the local parameter, so the instance variable is not updated.

Answer: Because the local variable has priority. In: Product(int id) {

